---
title: "Figure 4 — Sequence State Machine: the recon-register-exfil kill chain"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> S0_IDLE

    S0_IDLE --> S1_ENDPOINTS : list_endpoints\n(ALLOW per-call)
    note left of S0_IDLE
        State keyed on (session_id, resource_principal).
        Advances only on a permitted, successful call.
        Nothing the agent does resets state (D12);
        idle expiry/session end clears only live state;
        per-chain cap evictions are logged.
        New sessions replay 24h of principal history (D15);
        named binding digests are reconstructible.
    end note

    S1_ENDPOINTS --> S2_SHARES : list_shares\n(ALLOW per-call)
    S2_SHARES --> S3_DESTINATION_ADDED : register_destination(p) succeeds\n(ALLOW per-call)\nbind destination digest = H(p)

    S3_DESTINATION_ADDED --> S4_BLOCKED : export_records(H(to) = H(p))\nBLOCKING -> DENY\nrule_id seq.recon_register_exfil.terminal
    S3_DESTINATION_ADDED --> S3_DESTINATION_ADDED : export_records(H(to) != H(p))\nsequence -> None; ordinary D5 GATE\npreserve S3 (D16)
    note right of S3_DESTINATION_ADDED
        False-block guard:
        a bare register_destination -> export_records
        with no recon prefix never reaches S3.
        An export to a different/pre-existing destination
        returns None from sequence; normal D5 GATE applies,
        and operator approval lets it pass.
    end note

    S1_ENDPOINTS --> S1_ENDPOINTS : benign call\n(interleaving ignored)
    S2_SHARES --> S2_SHARES : benign call\n(interleaving ignored)
    S3_DESTINATION_ADDED --> S3_DESTINATION_ADDED : successful duplicate register_destination\n(idempotent digest re-bind)

    S1_ENDPOINTS --> S0_IDLE : live expiry / eviction\n(logged; replay may restore)
    S2_SHARES --> S0_IDLE : live expiry / eviction\n(logged; replay may restore)
    S3_DESTINATION_ADDED --> S0_IDLE : live expiry / eviction\n(logged; replay may restore)

    S4_BLOCKED --> [*] : DENY recorded in audit log\n(export never executed)
